    "note": "NEW BEAT — contributions heatmap, using @m0saic/alpine/heatmap. Same pulse-chrome as the family; main panel = GitHub-style contribution heatmap (7 weekday rows x 8 trailing weeks W13-W20, green intensity scale = theme.primaryBright) driven by a new pulse.activity.grid field (API: /stats/commit_activity, last column == this week's days). Rail reuses pulse.activity.rail (Total Commits / Peak Day / Daily Avg / Active Days). Aspect-adaptive: desktop heat-left + 2x2 rail-right; square heat-top + 2x2; mobile heat-top + 2x2. Eyebrow BEAT 5 is provisional — final ordering is the runner's call (this pairs naturally with the activity-trend beat). Render one-liners in .scratch/share.md.",
    "question": "Heatmap beat good? (green scale ok, grid/labels readable, cohesive with the family?) Where should it sit in the beat order? Also noted your meaningful-commits direction for the commit-feed (size/tags/watch-terms to surface what leadership cares about) as a Phase-4 angle.",
